## Original Content
Low-cost S&amp;P 500 index funds are the foundation of many portfolios to grow wealth, but investors should add assets to diversify and lower volatility.

## Summary
Low-cost S&P 500 index funds have been a reliable foundation for growing wealth, benefiting from the strong performance of the largest U.S. stocks. However, experts caution investors against getting greedy and recommend adding other assets to diversify portfolios and reduce volatility.

## Key Points
- Low-cost S&P 500 index funds are the foundation of many investment portfolios for building wealth
- The biggest U.S. stocks have delivered strong returns recently
- Experts warn investors not to become overly concentrated or greedy with large-cap U.S. equities
- Adding additional asset classes helps diversify holdings and lower portfolio volatility


